# a variant declaring no result beside variants declaring one is the default: a call no expected type tells apart takes
# it, a declared variable, a parameter, a declared result or `as` take the typed one (decision default-variant, user 11-11)
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; half 7'	3
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; y: float = half 7; y'	3.5
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; shown(v: float) := v; shown(half 7)'	3.5
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; g(n): float := half n; g 7'	3.5
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; (half 7) as float'	3.5
# arithmetic tells nothing: the default's result times a float
'half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; half 7 * 1.0'	3
# a told type no variant declares takes the default only where its result fits, else the usual type error
'class pdf { body: text }; half(x) := x /! 2; half(x): float := x / 2; p: pdf = half 7; p'	error	decision default-variant: p takes a pdf, not 3
# refused: two variants declaring no result, and a default whose known result a typed variant declares
'h(x) := 1; h(x) := 2; h(x): float := x / 2; h 1'	error	decision default-variant: a second definition of h taking as many arguments can never run
'k(x) := "a"; k(x): text := "b"; k 1'	error	decision default-variant: the k declaring no result gives a text, as its k: text does
